        "date": "2026-11-15T17:19:42Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(2d): Side Auto reads the material at the picked ring's own level\n\nSide Auto of a 2D Contour on picked rings read the full XY silhouette\nof the part. The floor of a blind bore fills that silhouette, so Auto\nresolved Outside on a bore rim and the #1927 law refused the pass.\n\nThe new law (machining2d::auto_side) reads the part section just under\nthe top of the picks' Z span, then just over its bottom, and compares\nthe area inside the rings with a 0.5 mm band outside them. Material on\none side only decides the side. Probes that disagree, or material on\nboth sides or on neither, refuse the generate by name and ask for\nInside or Outside.\n\nFixes #1933\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
